From: Q1000K development <q1000k@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: select the PON output queue for its T-CONT

The native PON API validates that its output queue matches the T-CONT channel,
but the descriptor submission path used the Ethernet device's fixed queue.
Derive the PON output queue from the validated channel in message word zero,
matching the Q1000K factory descriptor path. Keep the per-device selection for
ordinary Ethernet traffic. CPU DMA ring selection is independent of this field.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2789,7 +2789,12 @@
 	}
 
 	fport = airoha_get_fe_port(dev);
-	msg1 = FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_NBOQ_MASK, dev->nbq) |
+	/* Preserve the vendor PON output-queue selection for each T-CONT,
+	 * independently of the CPU DMA ring used for submission.
+	 */
+	msg1 = FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_NBOQ_MASK, pon_msg ?
+			 FIELD_GET(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_CHAN_MASK, *pon_msg) :
+			 dev->nbq) |
 	       FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_FPORT_MASK, fport) |
 	       FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_METER_MASK, 0x7f);
 	if (pon_msg) {
